signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in (1,4].$ The corresponding region is a trapezoid, so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{2}(a+b)h \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1+3)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The $4$th integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [4,7].$ The corresponding region is a quarter-circle of radius $3,$ so we find the area using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{4} & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\pi (3)^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}-{A}_{2}+{A}_{3}+{A}_{4} \\\\  & =\\pi -6-2+6+\\frac{9\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{13\\pi }{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{13\\pi -8}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330047 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\pi -12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330047 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330047 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0b429cbf-699c-5402-ba85-c66f431ab290" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330900 #edb/ref 1080 "4\\pi -6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330900 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186330900 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "69f7df2a-712e-5d88-8c8c-2c5d26706731" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331432 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\pi +12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331432 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331432 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a5a1bf43-831a-54f4-9b93-23a8155c13c6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331520 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}-12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331520 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331520 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b19a89e7-a647-5d27-a40a-536fedc46b9c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331851 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\pi }{2}+12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186331851 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb